'' 'select channel' BEHAVES as fbc's does: every case form, and every outcome that does
'' not depend on the scheduler, built to an executable. This test can only BUILD it --
'' the runner does not execute what it builds -- so build/goldenrun.sh is what runs it
'' beside fbc and compares the bytes; the source's header is fbc's output, measured.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -mt -target win64-msvc -i toolchains/tiko-windows/inc tests/driver/src/select-channel-run.bas -o tests/driver/selchanrun.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/win64-msvc
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/selchanrun.exe
'' EXPECT-NOT: undefined symbol
